    "title": "Gamecocks offensive line aims to be area of strength in 2026 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Katie Dikes ,\n23 hours ago During the nine games last season that ex-offensive coordinator Mike Shula coached, South Carolina did not have a winning record and was ranked last in the SEC in points, with 19.7, and in yards per game, with 294.1. Nothing may prove more important to this upcoming season's success than improvement on the offensive line. Read full article\n1",
